-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"c52f6e372aa93207e1188c378b11ac73608af7d92b85a3467106f18773edabb3","event_uuid":"36017f4c-cff0-4d61-9782-a6db0b8c0bf3","position":{"commit_sha":"59d58df34d833f910d067107960287ce036b0c19","position":"1786498784545369001-36017f4c-cff0-4d61-9782-a6db0b8c0bf3"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"rebar-bridge[bot]","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"BRIDGE_CANARY_ALERT: Bridge audit findings still present as of 2026-08-10T22:13:20Z: store_integrity=13. Run: https://github.com/navapbc/rebar/actions/runs/31437155060","timestamp":1786400002977029792},{"author":"rebar-bridge[bot]","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"BRIDGE_CANARY_ALERT: Bridge audit findings still present as of 2026-08-11T22:16:10Z: store_integrity=13. Run: https://github.com/navapbc/rebar/actions/runs/31541453937","timestamp":1786486572694838576},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"## Re-measurement (2026-08-11): the 13 enumerated. Still 13 — leaving OPEN. The 2fa6/re-clone attribution is wrong.\n\nRan `rebar bridge fsck` read-only against the live store (plus a direct `audit_store_integrity()`\ncall). No repair performed, no store state changed.\n\n### Current count: still 13, all one kind\n\n    unknown_event_types: []\n    binding_drift: would_terminal=0, local_gone=0, retired_overlap=0, dangling=0,\n                   unbound_jira=0, absent_in_window_unprobed=901, indeterminate=5\n    store_integrity: 13\n\nOnly `store_integrity` alerts. Every alerting `binding_drift` cell is already 0\n(`absent_in_window_unprobed` and `indeterminate` are non-alerting by design —\n`_engine_support/bridge_fsck.py:306`).\n\n### The enumeration asked for — all 13\n\nEvery finding is kind **`reverse_missing_forward`**: `bindings.json` has\n`reverse[<jira_key>] = <local_id>` with no matching `bindings[<local_id>]`.\n\n| # | kind | jira key | local ticket id | alias | status | type | title |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | reverse_missing_forward | REB-410 | b1c4-d00b-9212-4fa0 | barky-mulch-rave | deleted | epic | ZZ-RELTEST parent epic (DELETE ME) |\n| 2 | reverse_missing_forward | REB-411 | d53e-32bf-0d14-4c35 | rack-gourd-via | deleted | task | ZZ-RELTEST task Y (DELETE ME) |\n| 3 | reverse_missing_forward | REB-412 | f07e-84da-182d-4f96 | lit-scone-hoop | deleted | task | ZZ-RELTEST task X (DELETE ME) |\n| 4 | reverse_missing_forward | REB-413 | 950e-79da-f99c-474e | tusk-fan-teak | deleted | epic | ZZ-LINKTEST parent epic (DELETE ME) |\n| 5 | reverse_missing_forward | REB-414 | a220-e79d-f819-4e88 | rush-stump-matte | deleted | task | ZZ-LINKTEST task Y (DELETE ME) |\n| 6 | reverse_missing_forward | REB-415 | ec6a-cc65-f236-4fa1 | plop-seer-decay | deleted | task | ZZ-LINKTEST task X (DELETE ME) |\n| 7 | reverse_missing_forward | REB-416 | 94dc-264b-c6a4-41b5 | tepid-nil-karma | deleted | task | ZZ-BIDIRTEST Y (DELETE ME) |\n| 8 | reverse_missing_forward | REB-417 | c652-360b-9169-4982 | knit-bride-moon | deleted | epic | ZZ-BIDIRTEST parent (DELETE ME) |\n| 9 | reverse_missing_forward | REB-418 | cb65-f0cb-8061-411c | muggy-trait-scene | deleted | task | ZZ-BIDIRTEST Z (DELETE ME) |\n| 10 | reverse_missing_forward | REB-419 | eb3c-f55b-eacc-47b6 | good-twig-morel | deleted | task | ZZ-BIDIRTEST X (DELETE ME) |\n| 11 | reverse_missing_forward | REB-420 | 3f93-084b-1d4d-4dfb | plus-tea-mural | deleted | epic | ZZ-MLTEST E epic (DELETE ME) |\n| 12 | reverse_missing_forward | REB-421 | 9e39-ef9f-3dc9-4e9a | thin-peer-strip | deleted | story | ZZ-MLTEST M story (DELETE ME) |\n| 13 | reverse_missing_forward | REB-422 | f4dd-b7dd-8307-4bea | hump-chest-gang | deleted | task | ZZ-MLTEST L task (DELETE ME) |\n\nBy-kind histogram over the full `audit_store_integrity` vocabulary\n(`bridge_fsck.py:198-279`): `reverse_missing_forward` **13**; `forward_missing_jira_key` 0;\n`forward_missing_reverse` 0; `forward_reverse_mismatch` 0; `reverse_nonconfirmed_forward` 0;\n`reverse_jira_key_mismatch` 0.\n\nTwo structural facts worth recording: the Jira keys are a **perfectly contiguous block,\nREB-410 … REB-422** (REB-409 and REB-423 both have intact forward entries), and the store counts\nare `bindings`=2086 vs `reverse`=2099 — a delta of exactly 13. This is one event, not 13.\n\n### The 2fa6 / re-clone hypothesis does NOT fit — four independent counts against\n\n1. **Wrong provenance.** All 13 were created **2026-06-26T02:48Z** by author `Iso Tester` under\n   `env_id ade0f2ef-...`, a different environment from the current store (`01a1a015-...`). They are\n   isolated-test scaffolding, literally titled `ZZ-RELTEST / ZZ-LINKTEST / ZZ-BIDIRTEST / ZZ-MLTEST\n   … (DELETE ME)`, each archived ~21 minutes after creation (STATUS + ARCHIVED at 2026-06-26T03:09:42).\n2. **Wrong date.** The 2fa6 incident ([rebar:2fa6-e3cb-a11f-4e3d], git-stash-in-tracker) and its\n   re-clone tail ([rebar:eca3-d294-42f7-44b4], re-clone re-identifies the environment) landed in\n   early August 2026. This drift predates both by six weeks.\n3. **The gap never changed.** `.bridge_state/bindings.json` first appears in tracker history at\n   commit `1300f383c7` (2026-08-06, a COMPACT), and **its very first version already had exactly\n   these 13 orphans** (`bindings`=1815, `reverse`=1828, missing forward for REB-410…REB-422).\n   Sampling ~525 subsequent snapshot commits through 2026-08-12 shows the gap constant at 13 while\n   both indexes grew. The re-clone neither created nor widened it.\n4. **Not a retirement.** `bindings-retired.json` holds only REB-1585, REB-530, REB-695, REB-737,\n   REB-738, REB-877 — none of the 13. So `_retire()` (which correctly pops both indexes,\n   `binding_store.py:592-593`) is not the path taken.\n\n### Actual mechanism (best read)\n\nThe forward entries were dropped when those throwaway test tickets were purged/archived — most\nplausibly the `a3-remediation: batch 1` cleanup (2026-07-08, which mass-retired/archived event\nfiles) or an equivalent out-of-band prune — **without the paired `reverse` pop**. In current code\n`unbind()` (`binding_store.py:426-430`) only pops `reverse` when the forward entry still carries a\n`jira_key`, so any path that removes the forward entry by another route leaks the reverse key\npermanently. That asymmetry is the reusable finding here, independent of these 13 rows.\n\nSo: **stale bookkeeping for deleted test fixtures, not corruption from the tracker incident.**\n\n### Status: OPEN\n\n`store_integrity` is 13, not 0, so the ticket's own auto-close condition (\"auto-closes when bridge\nfsck next reports zero alerting audit findings\") is not met and I am not closing it. Stable at 13\nacross all three canary observations (2026-08-10T21:16Z, 2026-08-10T22:13Z, 2026-08-11T22:16Z) and\nmy run today.\n\nRemediation is now fully scoped and low-risk: delete 13 orphaned `reverse` keys (REB-410…REB-422)\npointing at deleted `ZZ-*TEST` fixtures. **No live ticket data is at risk** — every referenced local\nticket is `deleted` and was test scaffolding. Worth pairing with a look at the `unbind()` asymmetry\nabove so the leak cannot recur. Per this squad's remit I performed diagnosis only and did not repair.","timestamp":1786498784545369001}],"created_at":1786396581367109612,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[],"description":"## Reproduction Steps\n\nRun `rebar bridge fsck` — the offline bridge audit reports alerting binding\ndrift or a forward/reverse binding-store integrity inconsistency.\n\n## Expected vs Actual\n\n- **Expected:** alerting `binding_drift` cells and `store_integrity` are empty.\n- **Actual:** store_integrity=13\n- **Detected at:** 2026-08-10T21:16:20Z\n- **Canary run:** https://github.com/navapbc/rebar/actions/runs/31432828235\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Each reported drift is triaged (would_terminal → local archive/delete\n      to propagate; unbound_jira → adopt or archive the Jira-native issue;\n      local_gone → investigate; retired_overlap → remove the duplicate live/\n      retired membership; store_integrity → repair the inconsistent forward/\n      reverse index entries).\n- [ ] `rebar bridge fsck` reports empty alerting `binding_drift` cells and\n      `store_integrity`.\n\nThis ticket auto-closes when bridge fsck next reports zero alerting audit findings.","detected_by":"binding-drift-canary","env_id":"01a1a015-677b-4c9d-a5ad-d3187922b542","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["binding-drift-alert"],"ticket_id":"7f69-6d23-ff70-46ff","ticket_type":"bug","title":"[binding-drift] bridge fsck found 13 audit finding(s)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["b3e1e072-fe4d-48e1-9dca-db69b5ae5d4a","7e8dfe7d-9c17-4054-a76c-033a0c4c8552","46877c3f-c64b-4565-a9cc-c10fb977bf94","36017f4c-cff0-4d61-9782-a6db0b8c0bf3"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786498784545369002,"uuid":"45ea8a55-4822-44be-9445-52d2dded72b5"}